      "writtenOn": "2015-05-29T00:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we update tx_snapshot_head in __tx_char, then we\u0027ll run into infinite loops because EC_CMD_CONSOLE_READ will end up putting more characters into the buffer due to host commands and the \"+\" it sends over the console when transmitting data. I ran into this problem trying to implement the recent logs without having to piggy-back off SNAPSHOT commands.\n\nIt\u0027s a sad world, but since these commands are meant for debugging, I think there\u0027s a little bit of a lower bar for whether or not everything works perfectly. (At least, it seemed that much from the comments that were already here.)",
      "parentUuid": "ed56c9ec_a340fb14",
      "revId": "b490f39a2aea0e207be996cc0867e67f7dba6fa1",
